  "hits_capacity": 32,
  "theme": {
    "about": "Theme packages, format 1 (docs/theming_2026-09.md \u00a73-\u00a75, \u00a77). The seed packages are themes/<name>.json, embedded in the tables in this order; the first is the default every chain ends at. A missing role is derived per variant: the variant's own list first, then 'both', each [role, value] filling the role only when the chain left it unset (a value is a palette index, a flag, or another role). A role is a token (the live row apps read) or a 'content' role (code syntax and block colours, read by the Code and Blocks tabs). 'metrics' are the theme-wide metrics a package may set, each [min, max] (a value outside is clamped; the default seed sets every one). 'effects' are the text effects a part and state may name, at most 'effects_cap' per package. 'pairs' are the (background, ink) roles the readability check holds to 'contrast' (a WCAG ratio, x10) on the MOY64 table. 'bytes' caps a theme.json, 'depth' the inherits chain. A package's 'text' and 'surfaces' are keyed by part, then state: the parts are the kinds, then 'parts' (the chrome the WMs and the bar draw); the states are the style's, then 'states' (a window's), and a state a part does not name follows 'chain' to rest. A surface is one line of the grammar (docs/theming_2026-09.md \u00a74.4): an edge of 'edges', a fill of 'fills' with its colours, 'border' with an optional colour, 'shadow'; a colour is a token or a palette index. A package holds at most 'surfaces_cap' surfaces of at most 'surface_len' bytes each. A package's 'frame' chooses a window frame: 'style' one of 'frames', 'title_align' one of 'title_aligns', 'buttons' each letter of 'frame_buttons' once (close, minimise, maximise, the title), a '|' between them allowed; what it leaves out is its style's. A package's 'fonts' name a font file of the package per role of 'font_roles' (1 to 24 of a-z, 0-9, '_', '-', '.', not starting with '.'); the file's format is the font loader's (native/moy_gfx/moy_text.h). Each key of 'sheets' names a .moygfx file of the package (the same grammar, ending '.moygfx'), the cart sheet's hex format of at most 'sheet_rows' rows (docs/theming_2026-09.md \u00a74.6): 'sprites' is the ROLE sheet, each nibble a slot of 'sprite_slots' (null transparent, a token, or a palette index), its parts drawn from 'sprite_cells' ([part, state, title button of 'frame_button_names' or null, x, y, w, h] in 8-pixel tiles of a 128-wide sheet; a part of 'sprite_nine' is a 9-slice with 8-pixel corners), and 'icons' is the bar's IconSheet. A package's 'layout' holds 'bars' (docs/shell_layout_2026-10.md \u00a75): at most one bar per edge of 'layout.edges', each a 'size' clamped to 'layout.size' ('size_default' when absent); a 'home' names the home's arrangement, one of 'layout.homes', the first when absent or unknown, and the slots of 'layout.slots', each a list of at most 'slot_cap' names of 'layout.widgets', at most 'widget_cap' per layout; a widget placed twice keeps its first placement unless it is 'repeatable'; a bar's 'text' gives its 'text' widgets their strings by position, 1 to 'text_max' characters of printable ASCII. A layout that does not place every 'required' widget is refused, and the default's stands in. 'accents', 'tints' and 'recolour' are the accent-and-tint derivation's data (docs/theming_2026-09.md §4.10, moy_theme_derive): each accent is [name, A, deep], A one black clears; each tint is [name, its ramp of palette indices, dark to light, never 0 or 7]; 'recolour' names the role classes each of its steps rewrites: 'background' and 'line' take the tint ('line' only off black and white), 'accent' takes A and 'tied' takes A where the source tied it to its title or accent, 'accent_ink' the first of A, deep and ink that clears surface, each 'dim_ink' [role, its fallback, its backgrounds] the dimmest of the ramp and 'dim_greys' that clears them, and 'content' its derive-set value for the surface's side.",
    "format": 1,
    "seeds": ["night", "indigo", "berry", "forest", "slate", "machine", "platinum", "win95", "outline", "contrast"],
    "bytes": 4096,
    "depth": 4,
    "content": ["code_text", "code_keyword", "code_string", "code_number", "code_comment", "code_builtin", "block_events", "block_control", "block_actors", "block_looks", "block_draw", "block_input", "block_variables", "block_lists", "block_operators", "block_sound", "block_myblocks"],
    "metrics": {"radius": [0, 3], "press_dx": [-3, 3], "press_dy": [-3, 3]},
    "effects": ["none", "shadow", "emboss"],
    "effects_cap": 32,
    "parts": ["window", "window.title", "window.button", "bar", "bar.item", "desk", "desk.icon"],
    "states": ["active", "inactive"],
    "chain": {"disabled": "rest", "pressed": "hot", "hot": "rest", "on": "rest", "hover": "rest", "active": "rest", "inactive": "active"},
    "edges": ["flat", "raised", "sunken", "etched", "bevel2"],
    "fills": ["fill", "dither", "pinstripe", "gradient"],
    "surfaces_cap": 32,
    "surface_len": 48,
    "frames": ["classic", "tab", "platinum", "win9x", "flat"],
    "title_aligns": ["left", "center", "right"],
    "frame_buttons": "CMZT",
    "font_roles": ["ui", "title", "mono"],
    "layout": {
